-- RPC1: repair circle radii on CMP sections (any section whose channel is not TEM or SEM).
--
-- Older Viking builds copied a circle's radius into both MosaicShape and VolumeShape. CMP sections map into the volume at
-- about 30x, so the mosaic radius of those circles is about 30 times too large, and current builds (which draw from the
-- mosaic circle) show them as huge circles. Each row below keeps the mosaic centre (X,Y) and the volume radius the user
-- drew, sets the mosaic radius to the one whose forward mapping (five-point mean scale under the default transform
-- SliceToVolume1) gives that volume radius, and rewrites the volume cache from it.
--
-- Generated 2026-11-02 from OData (https://websvc.codepharm.net/RPC1/OData) and the volume's transforms
-- (http://rogue1.codepharm.net/RPC1/SliceToVolume.VikingXML) with Viking's LocationVolumeGeometry.
-- For every row the current transform maps X,Y back onto the stored volume position, which confirms the centre is right.
--
-- X, Y, VolumeX, VolumeY and Radius are computed columns, so only MosaicShape and VolumeShape are written.
-- Username and LastModified are kept: the Location_update trigger, which stamps LastModified, is disabled inside the
-- transaction and left as it was found before it ends (enabled again only if it was enabled). The script stops if
-- dbo.Location has any other enabled UPDATE trigger; disabled ones are ignored. While it
-- runs, its schema lock makes other edits to Location wait.
-- Each UPDATE matches the row's Version as read at generation time. If any row was edited since, the counts will not match
-- and everything is rolled back; regenerate the script then.
--
-- Run it in the RPC1 annotation database. It is a dry run unless @Commit is 1.
--
-- Not changed here, on purpose:
--   Sections 417 and 1048 (39 circles: 35 and 4) have no entry in SliceToVolume1, so Viking places them by identity and
--   their mosaic == volume geometry is consistent. If those sections are ever aligned, their annotations need mapping too.
--   Three circles whose section was re-aligned after they were drawn; the current transform moves their centre far from
--   where the user saw it, so the right radius is a judgement call:
--     220283 (section 460, c31996): centre moves 619 px, scale 34.3
--     114513 (section 565, c1245):  centre moves 21511 px, scale 61.5
--     183844 (section 565, c1217):  centre moves 13733 px, scale 64.3
--   399250 (section 712), saved 2026-10-30 by pulling through one of the oversized circles, is consistent (scale about 30)
--   but carries the oversized radius (volume radius about 1300); resize or delete it in Viking.
SET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON;
SET ANSI_NULLS ON;
SET XACT_ABORT ON;
SET NOCOUNT ON;
DECLARE @Commit bit = 0;
DECLARE @Expected int = 44;
DECLARE @Updated int = 0;

IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.triggers t JOIN sys.trigger_events e ON e.object_id = t.object_id
           WHERE t.parent_id = OBJECT_ID(N'dbo.Location') AND e.type_desc = N'UPDATE' AND t.name <> N'Location_update'
             AND t.is_disabled = 0)
BEGIN
    RAISERROR(N'dbo.Location has an enabled UPDATE trigger other than Location_update; review it before running this script.', 16, 1);
    RETURN;
END

BEGIN TRANSACTION;

DECLARE @ReenableTrigger bit = CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.triggers WHERE parent_id = OBJECT_ID(N'dbo.Location')
                                                  AND name = N'Location_update' AND is_disabled = 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END;
IF @ReenableTrigger = 1
    DISABLE TRIGGER dbo.Location_update ON dbo.Location;
